    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Bismuth quadruple therapy for 14 days, the best initial therapy where clarithromycin resistance = > 15% or unknown: a standard-dose PPI twice a day + bismuth subsalicylate 524 mg 4 × a day + metronidazole 250 mg 4 × a day + tetracycline 500 mg 4 × a day."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Clarithromycin triple therapy, only where clarithromycin resistance = known to be < 15% and w ⍉prev macrolide exposure: a PPI + amoxicillin 1 g twice a day (or metronidazole 250 mg 4 × a day) + clarithromycin 500 mg twice a day."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If quadruple therapy fails: ↓dose rifabutin + amoxicillin + a PPI, or vonoprazan + amoxicillin; ACG says ⍉clarithromycin triple therapy."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
